188
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:14,040
And I think this is where the policy conversation

189
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:15,420
is headed now.

190
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:18,270
And that means that there's a baseline of AI literacy.

191
00:09:18,270 --> 00:09:20,280
So, what is AI literacy?

192
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:24,220
And we do have that handy acronym,

193
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:30,090
PEOPLE, to remind us of the fundamentals.

194
00:09:30,090 --> 00:09:34,950
And that work on that acronym came from the AI Council,

195
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:38,160
which is a group of about 25 individuals

196
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:41,340
from all across the system in different roles.

197
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:45,637
A lot of faculty representation on that body.

198
00:09:47,550 --> 00:09:49,140
And it's been extremely helpful.

199
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:52,830
So, that's the group that developed the HUMANS Principles,

200
00:09:52,830 --> 00:09:56,070
but also PEOPLE which stands for,

201
00:09:56,070 --> 00:09:57,570
you know, prompting with purpose.

202
00:09:57,570 --> 00:10:01,380
That's the P. E is ethics first.

203
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:02,760
O is observe and verify.

204
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:04,560
This is my first public demonstration of this,

205
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,710
so we'll see if I can actually pull it off.

206
00:10:08,586 --> 00:10:09,767
- So far so good.

207
00:10:09,767 --> 00:10:11,640
- So far so good, right?

208
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:12,900
I just jinxed myself.

209
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:15,150
What's the second P, is,

210
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:18,270
oh yeah, we're kind of split on this one.

211
00:10:18,270 --> 00:10:21,690
So, the Chancellor said processor not person,

212
00:10:21,690 --> 00:10:23,520
AI council, you know, felt,

213
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:26,490
well, maybe we want to say personify wisely,

214
00:10:26,490 --> 00:10:29,430
but that second P is really about understanding

215
00:10:29,430 --> 00:10:33,720
that an AI is not a sentient individual, it's not a person.

216
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:37,440
And so kind of maintaining some emotional air gap

217
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:40,563
between yourself and that AI for your mental health.

218
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:45,120
And L, learn the basics.

219
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:48,750
So, we don't have to be computer scientists or AI experts,

220
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:49,980
Lord knows I'm not.

221
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:53,834
But if you understand the fundamentals of how a GPT,

222
00:10:53,834 --> 00:10:56,293
you know, an LLM works, the training,

223
00:10:56,293 --> 00:11:00,990
that can be very helpful to you as you become literate.

224
00:11:00,990 --> 00:11:03,630
And then E, committing to evolve continuously.

225
00:11:03,630 --> 00:11:06,371
Because obviously as we know, you know,

226
00:11:06,371 --> 00:11:09,840
every week, every month there's kind of a new advance

227
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:11,070
and something new happening.

228
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:15,150
And so just because something worked one way last month

229
00:11:15,150 --> 00:11:16,605
doesn't mean that's gonna be,

230
00:11:16,605 --> 00:11:17,900
you know, you can set it and forget it.

231
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:19,470
So that's our PEOPLE,

232
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:22,290
kind of the six fundamentals we feel all students,

233
00:11:22,290 --> 00:11:25,080
all faculty, all classified professionals,

234
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:27,510
all administrators should have that.

235
00:11:27,510 --> 00:11:29,430
So, how do we achieve that is really the question.

236
00:11:29,430 --> 00:11:32,160
How do we leverage policy to make AI literacy

237
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,910
something that's real for everyone?

